    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "The frai-core suite passes now: all 28 tests in 8 files. I changed two source files and didn't touch any test files.\n\n1. **Governance test** (`src/finetune/index.js`): the file used `APPROVAL_STATUSES` internally and in its default export, but never exported it by name. The test's named import came back `undefined`, so the `.join` call crashed. I added named re-exports for it and the other schema constants (`DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `DEFAULT_GOVERNANCE_TEMPLATE`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, `RISK_LEVELS`). The default export is unchanged. One side effect: these constants now also appear under the package's `Finetune` namespace.\n\n2. **Evaluation test** (`src/eval/metrics.js`): `runEvaluations` calls every metric with `(outputs, references)`. But the second parameter of `toxicityMetric` is `bannedTerms`, so the reference strings were being used as the banned words. Every output that matched its reference was flagged as toxic, which gave a score of 0. The fix wraps the toxicity entry in `DEFAULT_METRICS` so it only gets the outputs and uses the normal banned-word list. `toxicityMetric(outputs, bannedTerms)` still works the same when called directly.",
